# Binary assets — never apply line-ending (CRLF/LF) conversion to these.
#
# This matters for PDFs in particular: git guesses binary-vs-text by looking
# for a NUL byte in the first 8000 bytes, and a mostly-text PDF can have none,
# so git guesses "text". With core.autocrlf=true it then rewrites LF to CRLF
# on checkout, shifting every byte offset in the xref table and breaking the
# stream lengths — i.e. a silently corrupted, unopenable report.
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xls  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
